    "https://uni.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UNI/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Instruction---Psychology_JR1415": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction - Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current University of Northern Iowa employee and would like to apply for this position, login to UNI Works and type “Find Jobs” in the search bar to view and apply for open positions. Full Consideration Date: 10/23/2026 Job Description: The University of Northern Iowa's Department of Psychology seeks applications for a three-year term Assistant Professor of Instruction in Developmental Psychology position, starting in August 2027. This position includes a 4/4 teaching load, service expectations, and the possibility of renewal. The position requires teaching multiple sections of an undergraduate course in Developmental Psychology. Specialization within developmental psychology is open, but preference will be given to candidates who could contribute coursework to the department’s applied tracks, particularly those in school psychology and student affairs.  The Department of Psychology offers a B.A. degree centered on psychological science, with specialized applied tracks in mental health, behavioral health, work (I-O), military, school psychology, and student affairs. Education Requirements: M.A. in psychology or closely related field is required and a Ph.D. is preferred. ABD applicants with strong evidence of degree completion by August 2027 will be considered.  Required Qualifications: Compelling record of effective teaching, with demonstrated ability to teach Developmental Psychology required. Position Details: Job Category: Faculty Type of Position: Term Service Schedule: Academic Year For more information, please contact Nicholas Schwab, Search Committee Chair, at nicholas.schwab@uni.edu . Pre-employment background checks required. Applications Instructions: All application materials received by October 23, 2026, will be given full consideration. To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. The following materials must be attached when applying: 1) 