    "https://uni.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UNI/job/Main-Campus/Military-and-Veteran-Student-Services-Coordinator_JR1452": {
      "title": "Military and Veteran Student Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current University of Northern Iowa employee and would like to apply for this position, login to UNI Works and type “Find Jobs” in the search bar to view and apply for open positions. Full Consideration Date: 11/4/2026 Job Description: Summary: Coordinates student support services to promote the educational development and success of military, veteran, and military affiliated students; serves as an advisor and advocate for military,  veteran, and military connected students by providing information and education about admission, enrollment, career, transfer, financial aid, and counseling processes and services; provides mentorship, counsel and support for military,  veterans, and military connected students regarding transition to higher education; provides supervision to the Military & Veteran Services Center student staff; advises and collaborates with student organizations and leaders regarding event planning; and represents the University on local, statewide, and regional community boards, committees and other community initiatives. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree; at least three years of administrative or social work experience; excellent oral and written communication skills; demonstrated ability to build and maintain collaborative relationships; and strong problem-solving skills required. Occasional evening and weekend work will be necessary. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree; personal military experience; or experience working with military service members, veterans, or military affiliated populations in a university setting preferred. Position Details: Job Category: Professional and Scientific Type of Position: Regular Service Schedule: Calendar Year Application Instructions: All application materials must be submitted by November 4, 2026, to be considered for this position. To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Applicatio