    "https://uni.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UNI/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Adjunct-Professor---Science-Education_JR1457": {
      "title": "Assistant Adjunct Professor - Science Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nIf you are a current University of Northern Iowa employee and would like to apply for this position, login to UNI Works and type “Find Jobs” in the search bar to view and apply for open positions. Full Consideration Date: 10/29/2026 Job Description: The University of Northern Iowa’s Department of Science Education seeks applications for a temporary Assistant Adjunct Professor, starting in January 2027. This position will teach SCI ED 5500 Techniques for Science Teachers: Making Sense of Modern Science - From Headline to Phenomenon. This one credit hour course explores current scientific discoveries and emerging research reported in the news and examines the scientific principles, evidence, and questions underlying these developments. Mode of Instruction: Online with Zoom meetings from 7-7:50 pm on Wednesday evenings during the Spring 2027 semester. This position is eligible to be performed remotely within the state of Iowa. Employees who elect remote work must comply with the requirements of our remote work policy and agreement.   Required Qualifications: Master's degree in science education or related field plus relevant professional or practical-oriented expertise appropriate to the assignment required. For more information, please contact Larry Escalada, Search Committee Chair, at 319-273-7357 or e-mail at lawrence.escalada@uni.edu . Pre-employment background checks required. Position Details: Job Category:  Faculty Type of Position:  Temporary Service Schedule:  Spring semester Application Instructions:  All application materials must be submitted before 10/29/2026 to be considered for this position. To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. The following materials must be attached when applying: 1) Curriculum Vitae 2) Cover Letter You will have the opportunity to attach multiple documents when completing the application. Before submitting your online job ap